  Placement: 1
  CardStory: "Some of the smiles dwindle when the burnings begin.\r\n\r\nIt\u2019s
    just copied books, at first. 2Spade can\u2019t help but feel irritation at it.
    Strange orders are one thing, but this is just asinine. Irritation turns to worry
    when they start burning originals, though. Many of those tomes are worth more
    than he can imagine.\r\n\r\n*Paper is derived from cellulose, which is processed
    from wood. Wood is burned, sometimes stacked in deliberate patterns. It follows
    that paper would too. I understand.* \r\n\r\nWorry becomes fear when the orders
    extend to all written words, then any print. Holy scripture, personal correspondence,
    pictures and paintings. It comes to a head when 8Club refuses to hand over a
    family portrait. She is given death the same night, and her belongings destroyed.\r\n\r\n*Things
    that aren\u2019t wood can burn too.*"
